.Dd November 21, 2026
.Dt KSTAT 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm kstat
.Nd print typed kernel statistics
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl h
.Op Ar module:instance:name
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm reads the bounded DTrace per-CPU ring statistics through the existing
.Dv DTRACE_STATS
syscall and prints them as typed
.Dq module:instance:name
records.
The first consumer exposes the per-CPU
.Dq produced ,
.Dq consumed ,
.Dq dropped
and
.Dq capacity
counters plus checked global sums and the represented CPU count.
.Pp
The model uses 30-byte name components and the Illumos
.Dv KSTAT_DATA_*
types and units.
A malformed name is rejected with a stated error; a full
caller buffer or aggregate overflow is an error, never a wrap.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n
Emit one JSON object per line instead of the human
.Dq kstat: name=... type=... unit=... value=...
lines.
.It Fl h
Print usage.
.It Ar module:instance:name
Print only the exact named record.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kstat dtrace:global:produced
kstat: name=dtrace:global:produced type=uint64 unit=count value=17

$ kstat -n dtrace:cpu0:capacity
{"name":"dtrace:cpu0:capacity","type":"uint64","unit":"count","value":4096}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtrace 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
